Z||000006||Fiero5||05-24-2001||09:11 PM||||"What exactly is a "Fiero SS"? Is that anything like a VTEC Toyota Corolla?"<P>NO, it's not anything like that.<BR>I see the SS as one step above an SE and one step below a GT. <BR>However, if I keep fixing this baby up, it might end up being one step above a GT...Heh, heh<P>Steve<P>------------------<BR>                      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero9signature.jpg">                    <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||6
Z||000007||Black88GT||05-24-2001||09:52 PM||||Damn you stimpy you beat me to it.  <P>When I think "SS" I think Camaro SS with its muscle car heritage and muscle car motor.  When I think SS I think of the Chevelles with their big block motors and wheel spinning torque. <P>When I see SS on a stock Fiero, I think rice.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fiero2||05-25-2001||12:28 PM||||Steve is going to do mine for my "new" Fiero so it is custom like that also. <BR>BTW: My sig pic will soon change, as this is no longer my current ride. Waite till the surprise is revealed!<P>Marian Kelley<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/p9600001141effbe2f721d3cdf1c8091c/ff5ad888.jpg]http://www.zing.com/picture/p9600001141effbe2f721d3cdf1c8091c/ff5ad888.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000009||Fiero5||05-25-2001||12:34 PM||||"Wow, that looks great! Looks exactly like the one rodney dickman sells...except for the SS part. How'd you do that?"<P>You are right, it is one of Rodney Dickmans awesome spare tire covers. However, I worked with Rodney on what to use to get the Fiero GT lettered part of the printing cleaned off by carefully using laquer thinner. Then I had a custom made Fiero SS aplique that matched my other SS decals from Paul McKibben that I placed on it.<P>Steve<P>------------------<BR>                      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero9signature.jpg">                    <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||12
Z||000010||FieroHeather||05-25-2001||12:45 PM||||I really like your car FieroJoe.  That is a sweet colour you've got going there.<P>Black88GT:  I didnt know that you could turn a Fiero into a Ricemobile?  I thought only imports could become Ricers (with the extra sticker, exhaust tips, and tints of course)?<P>Fiero5: Nice wheel cover, it really cleans up the look of the trunk--less dirty looking in there that way, eh?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000011||LZeitgeist||05-25-2001||02:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Black88GT: I didnt know that you could turn a Fiero into a Ricemobile? I thought only imports could become Ricers (with the extra sticker, exhaust tips, and tints of course)?<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>It's no longer marque-specific... it's become a state of mind. <P>I realized this when I saw a teal Ford Probe (factory color) with yellow bodyparts here and there (obviously everything you could take off in an afternoon with only a screwdriver) and a big yellow graphic diagonally across the hood/front fender in Japanese Kanji script...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||1
