Z||000021||Black88GT||05-26-2001||03:37 PM||||I don't like it for the same reason I don't like stock Integra's with Type R Vtec SiR stickers.  It's kind of ironic how everyone on this forum will bash the hell out of a Teg/import with improper badging but when a Fiero does it they get the silent treatment.  I would probably feel differently if the car was powered by an LT1 or something similiar.  Also like Formula pointed out, there is no such thing as a Pontiac anything SS.  <P>Not to get off topic but its sad what the "SS" has become.  Seen the new Monte Carlo "SS"?  They didn't even give it the S/C version of the 3800.<P>Oh yeah, KissmySSfiero, you must not have been around for the infamous football thread in the O/T section.  Do a search for it, to my knowledge it has the most posts of any topic ever on PFF.  The subject is "Those tricky Buccaneers" started by Ricecooker.  Enjoy all my pics hehe<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 05-26-2001).]||||reg||11
Z||000022||KissMySSFiero||05-26-2001||05:41 PM||||Blackgt, Ive seen the thread but its too long for me.  maybe ill check someday.  i still hate the ravens because they left cleveland.  i do agree with the SS on the Monte Carlo.  why no SC3800.  gets me.  <BR>The only way KissMySSFiero will ever appear anywhere on my car is when i do a V-8 swap with TPI and i get a custom plate that has it.  but thats it.  i would rather have a sleeper anyways.  I guess KissMyGTPFiero doesnt have the same ring to it.  <P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000023||Fiero5||05-26-2001||06:46 PM||||Though the Tech 4 in this awesome Fiero is cranked up plenty and can take out most of the yahoos I meet at the lights and on the highway, I was thinking that since the SS does come from a muscle car era, I might want to slap something in the engine bay that is a little more in touch with the SS heritage.<P>My wife Marian (Fiero2) and I went to a big salvage yard today and looked at alot of different cars. I looked at a few Grand Ams that had quad 4's, and a few cars that had big V6's and so on.<P>I just need to find the right engine that will be an easy swap for this allready awesome beast, while staying within what I feel is appropriate for the SS on my car. Not that it isn't awesome enough to have the SS on it now, as it certainly is...  heh, heh, heh<P>Steve<P>------------------<BR>                        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero9supersig_1.jpg">                      <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||12
